  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (0.00) and model shows upward bias, especially after recent spikes.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes (e.g., >70.00) by applying a 5-10% downward correction to prevent overreaction.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction: if 3 consecutive forecast days exceed true outcome by >5%, reduce subsequent forecasts by 1-2% per day.",
    "When sentiment history shows a 0.33 (moderate bullish) but true outcome is lower, reduce forecast by 1-3% to account for sentiment overestimation.",
    "For 30-day horizon, if model consistently overpredicts by >2% over 3+ consecutive days, apply a 1-2% downward adjustment to avoid horizon bias.",
    "If true outcome is significantly lower than forecast (e.g., >10% below), consider a 2-5% downward correction to reflect market correction or supply/demand shift."
  ]
}
